From e7d7b1b2da10370b46b982bb280bc40a7176ae7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 07:47:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(multiaxis): Rotary Parallel cuts the full turn of the
 bar

The laid swarf raster finished the bar from above only: the bottom
quadrant counted as shallow ground that the raster never reaches, the
rings skipped it, and the ladder stopped at Bottom read as a tip height.
On a laid bar 126 degrees stayed uncut; on the example about a quarter.

The rotary path now plans the bar in two halves: the laid frame and the
same frame turned half a turn about the axis. Each half keeps the cut
over its own upper half, the turned half is carried back by the rigid
half turn, and the seam keeps each pass once. The turned half is held
to Bottom where the radial ball touches the bar, so a Bottom above the
axis still keeps the cut to the upper arc. The raster and ring notes now
reach the path, and a full-turn path says it needs a full turn of A.

build_sups and every shared finishing helper are unchanged. The example
program and project are regenerated with WRITE_GOLDEN=1; the guide page,
its pictures and its pins follow.

Fixes #2970

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
