From bfefff3bd65cfdf930e87a46d69a017421b22e67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:33:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(multiaxis): Rotary Parallel halves lose no
 single-frame cut

Review of PR #3650: on a part that is not round the plane seam dropped
cuts the single laid frame made - a keyway's lower wall, cut by half A
with its ball centre under the seam and out of half B's sight. A cut of
A under the seam now stays unless B cuts the same place (within half a
pass spacing); a cut of B over the seam is added where A cuts nothing
near (a wall that faces down). A reach reading on a fixed station x
angle grid names the arcs no pass reaches; only a path with none says
it goes all the way round. Round bars keep their output.

The test reference is the generator as it stood before the halves
(single_frame_tests.rs, test only): the keyed bar lost 52 centre samples
before this change and loses none now, and no place is cut twice. The
operations test bound reads each half's own law and the touch in world
z for every feed and plunge; a keyed bar in bar stock verifies clean.

Refs #2970

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
