From b4eda8a40e9e0a2b1de3f37cbd03030365896f64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:19:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] test(app): Rotary Parallel bounds that can fail, and the
 corner verdict

The per-half Bottom reads in operations.rs could not fail on that bar;
they are gone, and the world-z touch bound on every feed and plunge,
the counts of both halves and the sector check are the bounds (a Bottom
1 mm higher in the bound makes it red). The keyed bar accepts only the
envelope verdict at the keyway with its gouge within 0.05 mm. The
decision file states that the round outputs stayed the same on the run
fixtures, not by a law, and names the follow-up #3658.

Refs #2970

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/app/tests/operations.rs                | 18 +++++------
 crates/app/tests/rotary_parallel_keyway.rs    | 30 ++++++++++++-------
 docs/decisions/2970-rotary-parallel-halves.md | 15 ++++++++--
 3 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

